00:08:47.889 --> 00:08:52.409
Quantum error correction is the mechanism to take it apart, and the split is physical.

00:08:52.969 --> 00:08:54.549
The chip holds a fragile state.

00:08:54.949 --> 00:08:58.809
A classical machine has to name the error and the fix before that state drifts.

00:08:59.469 --> 00:09:05.309
HPC wires account of the November 5th announcement puts IBM Oak Ridge's Quantum Science Center

00:09:05.309 --> 00:09:07.709
and AMD on one bench for that split.

00:09:08.329 --> 00:09:14.729
IBM's Nighthawk brings 120 qubits, square lattice links, a high circuit rate, and pulse control

00:09:14.729 --> 00:09:21.069
that can act while a circuit is still running. Oak Ridge's Umbra, with AMD Instinct MI35X

00:09:21.069 --> 00:09:28.369
GPUs and 5th generation EPY CPUs, is the classical side. Together they let a team score each code

00:09:28.369 --> 00:09:34.209
by qubits, time, samples, and classical cost. On the quantum box, a researcher can measure

00:09:34.209 --> 00:09:39.869
mid-calculation and branch at once. Time the guard pulses, see what actually ran and work

00:09:39.869 --> 00:09:45.789
from the raw signal. Many noisy physical qubits stand in for fewer logical ones. The decoder

00:09:45.789 --> 00:09:50.789
reads the syndrome and names the correction. Late means the name no longer matches the state.

00:09:51.389 --> 00:09:56.129
Umbra is where that decoder gets tried on GPU nodes big enough to resemble a later machine

00:09:56.129 --> 00:10:01.769
and where codes get ranked by the classical load they impose. The announcement says the open question

00:10:01.769 --> 00:10:07.049
is no longer whether correction works on the hardware, but how to speed it. IBM's recorded

00:10:07.049 --> 00:10:13.729
experiments sit it up to 70 logical qubits and 438 hard operations. The Department of Energy's

00:10:13.729 --> 00:10:20.089
Quantum Genesis mission, through the Q competition, wants 100 logical qubits and 100,000 hard

00:10:20.089 --> 00:10:29.389
operations by late 2028. 70 to 100 is 30 more logical qubits, under half again. 438 to 100,000

00:10:29.389 --> 00:10:32.129
is the gap they call roughly 230 times.

00:10:32.609 --> 00:10:36.829
A decoder that keeps up for a few hundred operations has not shown it can keep up when

00:10:36.829 --> 00:10:41.189
every added operation is another measurement round and another classical decision.

00:10:41.729 --> 00:10:45.409
Nighthawk drops out of the experiment the day the code needs a hundred twenty-first

00:10:45.409 --> 00:10:50.889
physical qubit, or the day the question is 100,000 operations rather than 438.

00:10:51.529 --> 00:10:56.749
Until a larger quantum processor shares that bench, Umbra Prices methods, it does not

00:10:56.749 --> 00:10:58.649
deliver the late 2028 count.

